<!--
  Lint configuration.

  UseKtx is off on purpose, not by neglect. Every one of its suggestions asks
  for an androidx.core-ktx extension at a call site that already works without
  it, and this module keeps its dependency list as short as the platform
  allows — adding core-ktx to satisfy a style rule is the wrong trade.

  Left at warning level those ~35 entries are most of the report, and the
  point of a report is that a real error is findable in it.

  The remaining warnings are NOT silenced, because each one is a real question
  somebody has to answer:
  - ApplySharedPref (Prefs.kt): `commit` on purpose — the write broadcasts to
    system_server, so it has to have landed before the broadcast leaves.
  - DiscouragedPrivateApi (Hooker.kt): the whole module is reflection into
    ROM-private APIs; that is what it is for.

  Three groups that used to be reported here were removed rather than silenced,
  because what they described no longer exists:
  - IconMissingDensityFolder: it listed the three launcher-shortcut PNGs, which
    were density-specific (xxhdpi) while every other drawable was a vector, so
    the missing folders were not a gap in coverage. Those PNGs became adaptive
    icons (res/drawable/ic_shortcut_*.xml) and no density-specific drawable is
    left, so the rule has nothing to fire on.
  - UnusedResources: the XML token layer (`type.xml`, `shape.xml`, `dimens.xml`,
    `motion.xml`, `m3_emphasized_accelerate.xml`) restated the M3 type / shape /
    motion scale with no runtime consumer, so it only shipped a second copy of
    values `ComposeTokens.kt` already defines. Deleted once the last View screen
    became Compose.
  - ObsoleteSdkInt: version guards that minSdk 35 had made always-true. Each
    branch was folded into its single reachable path.
-->
<lint>
    <issue id="UseKtx" severity="ignore" />
</lint>
